  "body": "A new developer page, `site/content/developers/ai-agents.md` (\"Contributing with AI agents\", Developers section, after Releases). It is for outside contributors. It collects what we learned when we used Claude Code and other agents on this project. It gives no maintainer procedure.\n\nSections:\n\n- **Your first hour:** say hello on Discord, what to install (GitHub CLI, Rust, the Linux packages, an AI agent and its cost, disk), fork and clone, run the app with a sample part, a link to good first issues, and `/work-issue`.\n- **Getting started with Claude Code:** `AGENTS.md` is read automatically, the project skills, and the MCP server.\n- **From issue to main:** look at what is open first, claim by comment, branch, pinning test, quick gate, draft PR with the body checklist (`Changelog:`, `Fixes #N`, `Process change: yes`, screenshots on an images-only fork branch, a reason for a new test binary), review, merge. A series starts with its shape.\n- **Tips and gotchas:** disk per worktree, sccache and `CARGO_TARGET_DIR`, one gate for each checkout, failures that also fail on bare main, Windows and macOS notes.\n- **More than one computer** and **Using subagents.**\n- **Not a coder?** The issues are the backlog (read, comment, file good issues, check fixes). Contribute with designs (own models only, no vendor CAD).\n- **I have a CNC machine:** the shipped machine files and posts, what to send for a missing machine, and the first cut is an air cut.\n- **Clean room:** what we can use and what we cannot read (output, posts, tool libraries, screenshots or help text of other CAM products).\n- **Your agent helps with more than code**, **If something is unclear**, **We are all volunteers**, and a **FAQ** (no Rust, AGENTS.md is long, fear of breaking things, cost and time, small computers, machine owners, overwhelmed).\n- **Where to talk:** the CamCraft Discord and craftydevs.org.\n\nThree ideas are adapted from SolidCraft's contributor guide (Apache-2.0). The page credits them.\n\nThe page gives general learnings only. It has no machine names, accounts or private details. It says that `AGENTS.md` is authoritative.\n\nTested: `zola build` in `site/` passes (51 pages, no orphans), and the internal link to the AI guide page resolves. The reporter read the rendered page and approved it.\n\nChangelog: none\nRefs #3909\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAAAJyAPrC37zBzbbX\n",
